// RESEARCH DIAGNOSTIC ONLY.
//
// This successor joins the two previously separate research components:
//
//   1. the confirmed RSD v1.7 Macro broadening-wall selector; and
//   2. the v0.5.1 local paired-node consensus detector.
//
// The newest eligible Macro wall automatically supplies the immutable profile
// interval. Its same-side Far/Prior pivot is the start and its Outer pivot is
// the included end. Macro candle timestamps are refined to the exact 15-minute
// bars that printed the pivot prices. If either endpoint cannot be refined, the
// indicator abstains. No manual dates are required.
//
// The RSD adapter intentionally matches the v1.7 swing path with HTF confluence
// OFF. It uses confirmed pivots only, the pullback-tolerant two-sided wall gate,
// the Far-versus-Prior containment rule, and the existing steep-wall filter.
// The filter's ATR snapshot is latched when the confirmed Macro pivot tuple
// changes so an already-selected profile cannot churn on ordinary ATR drift.
// When both walls qualify, the wall with the newest endpoint wins; an equal
// endpoint prefers the longer span.
//
// Every retained profile boundary keeps the direction of its dense side.
// Starting at that anchor, each grid scans outward on the dense side and accepts
// the nearest material local maximum in opposite-direction clean strength that
// encloses a local volume bulge. A node is drawn only when the base-grid pair is
// complete and at least one neighboring grid agrees on both endpoints.
//
//   fine   = round(base row ticks * 0.8)
//   base   = base row ticks
//   coarse = round(base row ticks * 1.2)
//
// Each profile allocates every source bar's total volume by exact high/low tick
// overlap. The existing provisional local log-jump gates are applied to each
// grid independently. Anchor clustering keeps its configurable radius, while
// mate endpoints use the stricter fixed radius of one base row. Neighbor grids
// are evaluated pair-aware instead of inheriting the preselected standalone
// neighbor. Stable pairs rank by grid support, worst cross-grid node prominence,
// then the minimum anchor z score. Unpaired consensus anchors remain eligible
// as standalones. A selected pair consumes consensus anchors inside the node or
// within one consensus radius of either edge.
//
// Optional structural bounds can suppress otherwise-valid consensus shelves
// that are too close to the RSD range low or high. They are suppression inputs,
// not additional evidence.
//
// Source and endpoint contract:
//   standard 15-minute chart OHLCV only;
//   [Start 15m bar time, End 15m bar time + 15 minutes)
//
// This script does not create entries, exits, or support/resistance claims.
// It tests whether both edges of a volume node survive row-size perturbation.
indicator(
     "VP RSD Automatic Local Node Edge Consensus Diagnostic v0.6.0",
     shorttitle = "VP RSD AUTO 0.6",
     overlay = true,
     max_bars_back = 5000,
     max_lines_count = 500,
     max_boxes_count = 10,
     max_labels_count = 100)


